{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1019034-language-and-multilingual-merits-for-extinct-languages","id":1019034,"title":"Language and Multilingual Merits for Extinct Languages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-18T20:38:43-08:00","id":1019034,"title":"Language and Multilingual Merits for Extinct Languages","content":"Alright, so in some specific situations, the Language and Multilingual Merits may work exactly as described with dead languages. If a Sin-Eater finds the ghost of an ancient Egyptian scribe, she may get him to teach her the full Ancient Egyptian language, including speaking, reading, and writing.<br /> <br /> What about people who study dead languages like Latin, Sanskrit, Sumerian, etc, who have no viable way of learning how to speak them? How should the two Merits be interpreted for conversational fluency with context and full fluency?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T15:42:02-08:00","id":1019457,"title":"","content":"They probably learn those dead languages as the modern world reinterpretes them, not the original. This also probably means that there's room for both &quot;Sanskrit&quot; and &quot;True Sanskrit&quot;, or something like that.<br /> <br /> But then again, it's not like language is a static thing where it has evolution levels like Pokemon, so it'll be hard to translate every version of a language into Merits. In that case, I'd say the modern linguist who mastered Latin would have little trouble speaking with a ghost from the Roman Empire, even if the latter would be puzzled how the linguist speaks with this strange 'dialect' he never heard of before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T16:33:10-08:00","id":1019481,"title":"","content":"The modern interpretation aspect does seem important. Maybe a fair way to do it would be to say that anyone who studies a dead language can only achieve a Multilingual Merit-level fluency. Instead of being able to speak conversationally and read with context, they can read it well with context, and possibly write, but not speak it. Then only someone who learns the language from a ghost or other such ancient entity could get the Language Merit for it, which would grant the cultural knowledge for how it was used rather than just the mechanical knowledge, as well as things like authentic dialect, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T20:06:24-08:00","id":1019577,"title":"","content":"Chesh's interpretation also covers the excessive cost of learning a language that you won't ever have the opportunity to speak, since unless the said ghost appears, a dead language won't see much spoken use at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}